00:00:00.760 --> 00:00:04.550 align:start position:0%
 
[Music]  it's that time of the month again the  playstation plus games are here for  march 2022 and there's five of them so  we don't have time for this introduction  let's do this starting with the ps5 on  the ps5 we get our hands on gta online  to coincide with the release of the  enhanced version of gta 5. this isn't  the single player portion sadly it's  only the online aspect if you haven't  dropped into gta online before a new  career builder option is here for you  instead of slowly making a few dollars  on the street you'll have the funds to  buy one of many businesses on offer and  not be left behind by people who've been  playing for eight years plus there's  been 39 content updates over the years  so even if you have played but dropped  off there's something new for everyone  even dr dre is somehow in the game now  all the visuals have been updated with  4k 60 frames per second support and  tweaks to the aging control system which  should bring it in line with more modern  games oh and those loading times they  are so much more improved we get this on  the day it releases which is march 15th  then we have ghost runner a hugely  underrated free-running melee game which  is sublime the speed and complexity of  the moves you'll be pulling off after  only a few hours is jaw dropping we are  a lightning fast assassin running  constantly where a single bullet can  bring an end to your run this game has a  tough learning curve to help against  being shot we have the ability to slow  down time to take in the whole scenario  before jumping back into warp speed we  have a grappling hook and some ultra fun  cyber abilities to choose from in my  opinion ghost runner shouldn't be missed  depending on who you are the game is  extremely difficult and can be tough so  take a break if you're getting  frustrated but always know each time you  pass a room or zone your spawn will  update so you'll never have to go there  ever again as long as you go in being  prepared for a challenge and constant  dance music to keep you on edge you'll  have fun brutally hard at times but  hugely rewarding too next we have a  playstation multiplayer spin-off from  the brilliant ghost of tsushima this is  legends playing as a samurai hunter  ronin or assassin you'll battle through  japanese mythology you can do this alone  but it's the cooperative element that  makes this title stand out going  back-to-back with a friend in a  last-ditch standoff to claim a capture  point or planning the perfect approach  in an online squad working together to  fend off demonic foes and reviving  fallen comrades mid-battle really adds  to the drama like the single-player game  timing and reacting are much more  important in battle than simply smashing  as many buttons as you can and to make  us aware of this the progression system  leans into it it rewards us with moves  and techniques via a skill tree on  release day there was nine maps to play  through each with a different link to  the mythology of ancient japan and each  map has three variations to play through  bronze silver and the coveted gold oh  and as it's online expect a crazy amount  of cosmetics to stand out from your team  and emote too some of which are just  wrong in all the right ways on the ps4  now and arc survival evolved a survival  action title set in the prehistoric land  when dinosaurs were a regular occurrence  you awake on an island luckily you have  enough clothing to cover your junk but  that's about it it's now your job to  stay alive while getting to know the  island each day you get through is one  day closer to technological advancement  you'll go from throwing a spear at a  dinosaur on day one to sniping t-rex's  with a custom bolt-action rifle one day  playing in either third or first person  the core game is scavenging and building  somewhere safe to live alone this is  tough but with friends the game really  shines and if you choose to do this  online has 64 player servers to occupy  and the thing is trust do you trust the  other 63 players here as at any moment  they can stab you in the back literally  scores average at seven out of ten but  there has been many add-ons both free  and paid over the years which changed  the experience i've always wanted to try  this on playstation so i'm gonna jump in  how about you and then we have another  game sonic is here but it's not the  sonic you're thinking of it's team sonic  racing a mario kart style racer with a  few new ideas the core of every sonic  game is to go fast and here speed is in  abundance sonic racing uses a team  approach and expects you to act like a  unit sticking together the car in front  leaves a slipstream which lets the  others slingshot past before they return  the favor it's like a game of leapfrog  with your teammates whilst racing other  than that it's like mario kart with the  usual projectile items traps and speed  items to grab with online and local  multiplayer there's more life to sonic  team racing than you may expect so  that's the month of march what say you  do me a favor rank them in the comments  i'm adam you're awesome see ya

